rname>O'Neil</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Melega</surname><given-names>WP</given-names></name><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prolonged exposure of rats to intravenous methamphetamine: behavioral and neurochemical characterization</article-title><source>Psychopharmacology (Berl)</source><year>2005</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>501</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15959831</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00213-005-2188-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Oritani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimotouge</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishida</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Quan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujita</surname><given-names>MQ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Methamphetamine-related fatalities in forensic autopsy during 5 years in the southern half of Osaka city and surrounding areas</article-title><source>Forensic Sci Int</source><year>2000</year><volume>113</volume><fpage>443</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10978660</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0379-0738(00)00281-4</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>